STEP 7 — RISK
[RISK] sipgate: 38 — Broad REST v2 API (144 endpoints; voicemails, SMS, CDR history, portings, balance/payment, contacts) exposes per-user and global object IDs that are classic cross-tenant BOLA surface, but every endpoint is OAuth-scope-gated and no unauth bypass is demonstrated; true BOLA requires a valid test token (AUTH_HELPED). The OAuth implicit flow POST-login unvalidated redirect is real code but, statically, same-origin-only (no token exfil). redirect_uri prefix validation under app.sipgate.com is correct hardening that nevertheless maximizes ATO blast radius from any SPA XSS. No confirmed in-scope vulnerability this (passive) cycle; risk concentrated on the unconfirmed BOLA object-ID trust and the browser-gated redirect behavior.
